WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.834
-Our next guest is a talented
musician and actress

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:04.868
you know from shows
such as "Lizzie McGuire"

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:06.234
and "Younger."
She both produces --

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:09.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:00:09.434 --> 00:00:11.400
"Brideshead Revisited"
didn't do as hot.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:17.868
She both produces and stars
in "How I Met Your Father,"

00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:19.267
which is available on Hulu,

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:21.067
with new episodes
releasing on Tuesday.

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:22.167
Let's take a look.

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:24.167
-Oh, I'm so happy you're home!

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:25.267
I missed you so much.

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:26.667
-We don't have time for
"I miss yous"!

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:27.834
Dish.
How was your date with Ian?

00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:29.200
Was he tall?
-Yes.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.567
-Was he a good listener?
-Yes.

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:34.000
-Were his eyes
as kind as his photo?

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.234
-Yes!

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.834
-Whoooo!

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:40.367
Why aren't you jumping?

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:44.300
-Because he's moving
to Australia.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:48.834
Yeah.
-Soph, I am so sorry.

00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:51.701
Did you bang one out anyway?

00:00:51.701 --> 00:00:54.033
-Please welcome back to the show
Hilary Duff!

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:55.901
Hello, Hilary!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:55.901 --> 00:01:00.934
-Hi, Seth Meyers.
How are you?

00:01:00.934 --> 00:01:03.033
-It's so lovely to see you.

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:05.167
-Oh, my gosh, thank you so much.

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:06.968
So happy
to be on the show again.

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:09.300
What took you four years
to invite me back, huh?

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.901
-I know.
It's really odd.

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:12.634
I'm gonna take it up
with the talent department.

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:15.234
I'm pretty upset.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:17.267
You haven't --
Let me just say this.

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:20.200
It's been four years.
You haven't aged a day.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.734
You look fantastic.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:21.734 --> 00:01:23.434
-I had a lot of hair and makeup
to help with that,

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:25.767
but I definitely have.

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:27.501
-Well, one thing,
in the four years since

00:01:27.501 --> 00:01:30.501
I've last seen you, you have
added two more children.

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:32.434
Congratulations on that.

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:34.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:35.868
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:39.167
Sometimes I ask myself why, but
for the most part, it's good.

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:40.334
You just added one, too, right?

00:01:40.334 --> 00:01:41.801
-Yeah.
So, we've got a 4-month-old,

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:44.434
and I think that is
the conversation my wife and I

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:48.501
have every day, which is we love
her, but we're also, "Why?"

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:51.934
-Yeah, you can't not love them.
Like, they're insanely cute

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:53.767
and lovable but, you know,
you're like,

00:01:53.767 --> 00:01:55.534
"Wait.
We had a good thing going here.

00:01:55.534 --> 00:01:57.467
What were we thinking?"
[ Laughs ]

00:01:57.467 --> 00:01:59.801
-So how --
Your oldest now is 9?

00:01:59.801 --> 00:02:02.133
Is that right?
-He is, he is.

00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:04.100
-How is he with having
two babies around?

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:06.767
-He'll be 10 in March.
-...or two little ones around?

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:09.334
-How is with it?
-Yeah.

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:11.334
-He's, honestly, the best.
-That's great.

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:15.567
-He loves babies,
he loves little kids.

00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:17.067
He's so good with the girls.

00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:20.200
But he's my child that's just,
like, all good inside.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.067
And my middle daughter, like,

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:25.200
probably the house is
gonna burn down at some point.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.033
Like, she's just a wild one.

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:31.400
But we love her,
and it's so much fun.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:34.534
It's just, you know --
The no sleep?

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:36.400
I heard you don't get
your sleep back

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.601
until your youngest child is 6.

00:02:38.601 --> 00:02:40.868
You start recouping sleep,
and that sounds,

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:43.400
like, really faraway away.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:46.067
-Yeah, I had my kids later in
life, so I think, in six years,

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:48.834
I won't be regaining sleep,
I'll just be starting to die.

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:50.734
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, maybe that's --

00:02:50.734 --> 00:02:52.968
maybe that's
what's gonna happen to you.

00:02:52.968 --> 00:02:55.367
-So I heard --
You know, I'm very fascinated

00:02:55.367 --> 00:02:58.334
by the skills people picked up
during the pandemic.

00:02:58.334 --> 00:03:01.601
Guitar?
Is this true?

00:03:01.601 --> 00:03:04.601
-It's totally true
that I started taking

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:07.734
Zoom online guitar lessons.

00:03:07.734 --> 00:03:08.734
Shout-out to Teague.

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:11.300
What's up?
Miss you, buddy.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:14.300
My husband had bought me
a guitar for my birthday --

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:16.467
my 30th birthday --

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:18.734
and I didn't pick it up
for three years.

00:03:18.734 --> 00:03:22.167
And then I started playing,
and I can't remember anything,

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:25.234
but if I took a class, I think
it would still be in there.

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:30.267
So, we started with funny, like,
theme songs to old movies

00:03:30.267 --> 00:03:33.334
and TV shows, so I can play,
like, "Batman"

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:35.601
and "Mission: Impossible"

00:03:35.601 --> 00:03:38.734
and very easy,
simple, simple things.

00:03:38.734 --> 00:03:42.033
And I learned
the White Stripes song.

00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:43.501
[ Imitating
"Seven Nation Army" ]

00:03:43.501 --> 00:03:45.100
-Oh, yeah, the "Nation Army."
Something?

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.834
-"Seven Nation Army."
-How many nations?

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:48.801
One of them.
A number of nations.

00:03:48.801 --> 00:03:50.300
-But please don't ask me
to do it for you,

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.534
because I will fail miserably
right now.

00:03:52.534 --> 00:03:53.834
-Well, this is very exciting.

00:03:53.834 --> 00:03:55.067
There's a stranger
in your house,

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:56.501
and he's about
to hand you a guitar.

00:03:56.501 --> 00:03:59.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:00.834
I heard --
This is very exciting.

00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:02.868
You made an appearance
on a very popular show

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:06.167
that is dear to you,
"The Bachelor."

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:08.934
-Yeah. Yeah,
it is very dear to my heart.

00:04:08.934 --> 00:04:10.167
It's not yours?
-How did it come about

00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:13.467
that you got to appear
on "The Bachelor"?

00:04:13.467 --> 00:04:14.968
-Um, you know what?

00:04:14.968 --> 00:04:16.634
I think it was just promo
for the show.

00:04:16.634 --> 00:04:20.033
It was, like, tossed out there
with the promo packet,

00:04:20.033 --> 00:04:22.801
if you will, of, like, options.

00:04:22.801 --> 00:04:25.234
And my publicist was like,

00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:27.167
"I'm sure you're not gonna
be so into this."

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:30.200
And I was like, "What?!
Why would you think that?

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.234
Like, you don't know me
at all?!"

00:04:32.234 --> 00:04:34.234
Like, I actually love
"The Bachelor,"

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:37.434
and I haven't watched
in about a year,

00:04:37.434 --> 00:04:41.000
but we can blame
my youngest child for that.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.567
But, yeah, I've been fascinated
by "The Bachelor"

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:44.701
for a really long time.

00:04:44.701 --> 00:04:48.367
So getting to go
and be on set and have them,

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:51.534
like, take my phone away
from me, I felt really cool.

00:04:51.534 --> 00:04:52.834
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:55.734
-It's just top --
everything's top-secret.

00:04:55.734 --> 00:05:01.133
There's maybe 75 producers,
like, running around with, like,

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:03.167
ear things in and --

00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:05.067
But everything's
just unfolding naturally.

00:05:05.067 --> 00:05:06.868
Like, I don't know.

00:05:06.868 --> 00:05:09.267
I thought there was gonna be,
like, a script and a this.

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:10.667
It's not really like that.

00:05:10.667 --> 00:05:14.834
It is a, like,
social experiment.

00:05:14.834 --> 00:05:16.934
Maybe we're all in a simulation.
I don't know.

00:05:16.934 --> 00:05:18.534
It was fascinating.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:22.133
-I only watched one season,
and I got in way too deep.

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:23.267
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.267 --> 00:05:25.200
I was way
too emotionally invested,

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.567
and I realized,
"I don't think I'm prepared

00:05:27.567 --> 00:05:30.100
to take this journey again."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.234
-Was it "The Bachelor"

00:05:31.234 --> 00:05:32.467
or "The Bachelorette"
that you watched?

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:34.434
-I think I watched a
"Bachelorette" season.

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:37.067
And I think --
-Both equally as satisfying,

00:05:37.067 --> 00:05:39.234
so you can't really go wrong.

00:05:39.234 --> 00:05:42.267
It's just, can you get in,
and can you stay there?

00:05:42.267 --> 00:05:44.534
-"Satisfying"
isn't a word I'd use.

00:05:44.534 --> 00:05:46.033
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, okay, okay.

00:05:46.033 --> 00:05:47.868
-Like, I found --
Like, the way --

00:05:47.868 --> 00:05:49.601
I feel like -- I don't know.
I feel like,

00:05:49.601 --> 00:05:52.167
I've never done crack,
but I feel like if I did,

00:05:52.167 --> 00:05:54.767
I wouldn't say like,
"That was very satisfying."

00:05:54.767 --> 00:05:56.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.868 --> 00:05:58.334
It's, like, addictive.

00:05:58.334 --> 00:06:00.567
-I'm with you there.
I'm with you there.

00:06:00.567 --> 00:06:02.534
I maybe used the wrong word.

00:06:02.534 --> 00:06:05.334
I also have not used crack.
-Yeah.

00:06:05.334 --> 00:06:06.834
-But sometimes watching
"The Bachelor"

00:06:06.834 --> 00:06:08.267
does feel that way.

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:11.601
-Well, it seems like we have
our resolutions for next year.

00:06:11.601 --> 00:06:14.767
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.767 --> 00:06:17.968
So, "How I Met Your Father."
This is not --

00:06:17.968 --> 00:06:19.534
I think a lot of people
might assume from the title

00:06:19.534 --> 00:06:21.400
this is a reboot of
"How I Met Your Mother,"

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:24.834
but is it safe to say
it's a sequel of sorts?

00:06:24.834 --> 00:06:26.968
-I think so.
I think that's kind of

00:06:26.968 --> 00:06:28.734
how we're presenting it,

00:06:28.734 --> 00:06:31.434
because it's
a completely original cast,

00:06:31.434 --> 00:06:34.868
and, you know, we're not, like,
picking up where they left off.

00:06:34.868 --> 00:06:38.167
We're not -- you know,
my character isn't Ted Mosby.

00:06:38.167 --> 00:06:43.300
Like, we are new people
going on our new life adventure,

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:46.033
figuring out things at 30.

00:06:46.033 --> 00:06:49.133
But it ends the episode
in a really cool way

00:06:49.133 --> 00:06:52.367
that I think people will
understand our take on the show.

00:06:52.367 --> 00:06:54.801
And you know, obviously,
borrowing --

00:06:54.801 --> 00:06:57.234
it's such a great concept
to be telling your kid

00:06:57.234 --> 00:06:59.734
the story of how you met
their parent,

00:06:59.734 --> 00:07:03.701
and now it's being told
from the female perspective.

00:07:03.701 --> 00:07:10.234
And, yeah, we play with
a lot of, like, flashbacks

00:07:10.234 --> 00:07:12.534
and flash-forwards,
which tells a story, like,

00:07:12.534 --> 00:07:14.767
very quickly
and brings a great energy.

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:17.801
But it really is its own show,
and, you know,

00:07:17.801 --> 00:07:20.934
it's about 30-year-olds
doing life at 30

00:07:20.934 --> 00:07:24.367
and what that looks like now
in the age of online dating

00:07:24.367 --> 00:07:28.334
and limitless options and being,
like, swipeable.

00:07:28.334 --> 00:07:31.734
It's just completely stressful.
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:31.734 --> 00:07:33.200
-But, also, you know,
it's a love story

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.033
between a group of friends
that are kind of

00:07:35.033 --> 00:07:37.534
a pack of weirdos that all
love and accept each other

00:07:37.534 --> 00:07:39.834
and are just...

00:07:39.834 --> 00:07:42.000
you know,
trying to figure out their 30s

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.467
and what they want out of life.

00:07:43.467 --> 00:07:46.100
-You have a very cool
narrator in the show.

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:47.601
That was obviously a big part

00:07:47.601 --> 00:07:50.100
of "How I Met Your Mother,"
as well, and it's Kim Cattrall,

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:52.534
who is one of the coolest people
in the world.

00:07:52.534 --> 00:07:54.234
Did you actually
get to hang out with her

00:07:54.234 --> 00:07:56.634
since she was sort of
a narrator role?

00:07:56.634 --> 00:07:59.400
-Yeah, I spent
a little bit of time with her,

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.868
and she's --
she's a beast, man.

00:08:01.868 --> 00:08:04.501
She shot like 10 episodes
in one day.

00:08:04.501 --> 00:08:07.701
Like, all of her stuff
was really fast,

00:08:07.701 --> 00:08:11.033
but she just showed up
and kind of schooled us all.

00:08:11.033 --> 00:08:13.367
It was like, "Oh, damn.
That's how you do it," you know?

00:08:13.367 --> 00:08:15.567
She's such an icon.

00:08:15.567 --> 00:08:17.767
And I wasn't supposed
to be at work, and I'm like,

00:08:17.767 --> 00:08:19.868
"Oh, come hell or high water,
I'm showing up."

00:08:19.868 --> 00:08:22.234
Like, "Out of my way.
Where's Kim?"

00:08:22.234 --> 00:08:24.567
[ Laughter ]
And, you know, it's really cool

00:08:24.567 --> 00:08:30.067
to have her play the future
Sophie and tell that story.

00:08:30.067 --> 00:08:32.701
She's really witty,
but she's, like, warm and open.

00:08:32.701 --> 00:08:36.934
And there's something comforting
about having her tell the story

00:08:36.934 --> 00:08:40.701
and actually seeing her,
because, I don't know about you,

00:08:40.701 --> 00:08:43.534
but it would be so nice
to see the future me

00:08:43.534 --> 00:08:45.067
and know that I turned out okay.

00:08:45.067 --> 00:08:47.367
I made some good choices
that got me to the right places

00:08:47.367 --> 00:08:49.334
in life at that point.

00:08:49.334 --> 00:08:53.701
So there's that, like, comfort
in that part of the show,

00:08:53.701 --> 00:08:55.434
which she's obviously
a big part of.

00:08:55.434 --> 00:08:57.968
So, also, the show takes place
in New York,

00:08:57.968 --> 00:09:01.400
and when I think of Kim,
I think of New York City.

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:03.400
-Yes.
-So it's a cool element.

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:04.701
-Hey, thank you so much
for being here.

00:09:04.701 --> 00:09:06.767
I do hope, next time,
we can get you back in the city.

00:09:06.767 --> 00:09:09.534
-Um, well, I really hope that
next time you actually invite me

00:09:09.534 --> 00:09:11.734
to go day-drinking with you.
That's what I really want.

00:09:11.734 --> 00:09:13.000
-All right,
but here's the thing.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:14.200
Wait a second.
-I also haven't gotten

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:16.300
that invitation.
-All right, Hilary, but I think

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:17.601
a lot of people
want to do day-drinking.

00:09:17.601 --> 00:09:19.133
They think,
"Oh, it's fake or phony,

00:09:19.133 --> 00:09:21.701
and you do shots of water."
This is a real thing.

00:09:21.701 --> 00:09:23.334
-I don't think
you know me very well, Seth.

00:09:23.334 --> 00:09:26.033
Let's go.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:26.033 --> 00:09:29.234
It's on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:29.234 --> 00:09:31.000
-Hilary Duff, everybody.
New episodes of

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.801
"How I Met Your Father"
are available Tuesdays on Hulu.

00:09:33.801 --> 00:09:35.133
We'll be right back.

